This agreement is between **{{parties.company_name}}** of {{parties.company_address}} ("the Company") and **{{parties.supplier_name}}** of {{parties.supplier_address}} ("the Supplier"), an individual engaged to provide services under this agreement.

In this agreement:

- **the Services** means the services described in the next section and in Schedule 1;
- **an Assignment** means a specific piece of the Services agreed under the section on agreeing work;
- **Supplier Personnel** means the Supplier and any other person who provides the Services for the Supplier as this agreement permits;
- **the client** means a customer of the Company at whose site, or for whom, the Services are provided.

Schedule 1 (Key particulars) forms part of this agreement.

This agreement is between **{{parties.company_name}}** of {{parties.company_address}} ("the Company") and **{{supplier.name}}**, a company registered in {{supplier.registered_in}} under number {{supplier.number}}, whose registered office is at {{supplier.address}} ("the Supplier").

In this agreement:

- **the Operative** means {{operative.name}}, the individual whose services the Supplier provides;
- **the Services** means the services described in the next section and in Schedule 1;
- **an Assignment** means a specific piece of the Services agreed under the section on agreeing work;
- **Supplier Personnel** means the Operative and any other person who provides the Services for the Supplier as this agreement permits;
- **the client** means a customer of the Company at whose site, or for whom, the Services are provided.

{{supplier.signatory}}, {{supplier.signatory_title}}, signs this agreement for the Supplier and confirms that they are authorised to do so. Schedule 1 (Key particulars) forms part of this agreement.

The status assessment must be repeated, and this agreement reviewed, before a change takes effect or as soon as either party becomes aware of it, if:

- the Services, duties or sites change significantly;
- the Company or a client starts to supervise, direct or control how the work is done, or stops doing so;
- the work settles into a regular pattern, or either party starts to expect work to be offered or accepted;
- what happens in practice when Supplier Personnel cannot attend, or who provides the equipment, changes;
- the Supplier stops working for other customers, or its business structure changes;
- this agreement is extended or renewed.

The Supplier must tell the Company promptly about any change on its side. The Company is responsible for carrying out the reassessment and will tell the Supplier the outcome in writing.

The status assessment must be repeated, and this agreement reviewed, before a change takes effect or as soon as either party becomes aware of it, if:

- the Services, duties or sites change significantly;
- the Company or a client starts to supervise, direct or control how the work is done, or stops doing so;
- the work settles into a regular pattern, or either party starts to expect work to be offered or accepted;
- what happens in practice when the Operative cannot attend, or who provides the equipment, changes;
- the Operative is replaced, or the Operative's ownership or control of the Supplier changes;
- the Operative is placed with a client who directs the work, rather than working as part of the Company's own service;
- the Company's size under the off-payroll working rules changes;
- this agreement is extended or renewed.

The Supplier must tell the Company promptly about any change on its side. The person named in the section on tax is responsible for the reassessment, and the outcome will be given in writing, with a new status determination statement where the off-payroll working rules require one.
